---
/**
 * Terms of Use.
 *
 * Written against what the site actually does today, not against what it is
 * planned to do. There is nothing to buy here, no account to hold and nothing
 * to upload, so there are no clauses about any of that; when those arrive the
 * terms get a new version rather than a clause written early and left to rot.
 *
 * The licence section is the one place this has to be exact, and it follows
 * ATTRIBUTION.md rather than asserting a blanket claim: one of the three plates
 * is share-alike, which obliges us as much as it obliges anyone downstream.
 */
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';

const TERMS_VERSION = '1.0';
const LAST_UPDATED = '7 September 2026';
---

<Doc
	title="Terms of Use — The Itti Foundation"
	description="The terms on which The Itti Foundation offers this site, what you may do with what is on it, and what it is not."
	eyebrow="Terms of Use"
	heading="The terms of this site."
	lede="What this site is, what you can do with it, and what it does not claim to be."
	version={TERMS_VERSION}
	updated={LAST_UPDATED}
>
	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">Who offers this site</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				The Itti Foundation, registered as Itti&rsquo;s Skill School Foundation, a
				Section 8 not-for-profit in India. Where these terms say <em>we</em>, that is
				who they mean. Where they say <em>you</em>, they mean whoever is reading the
				site.
			</p>
			<p>
				Using the site means these terms apply to you. If you do not want them to, the
				remedy is not to use it.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">What this site is</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				An account of what the Foundation works on, and a form that lets you tell us who
				you are so we can reach you.
			</p>
			<p>
				That is the whole of it today. There is nothing to buy, no account to hold, no
				password, and nothing for you to upload or publish. Where the navigation points
				at parts of the site that do not exist yet, they do not exist yet. When any of
				that changes these terms change with it, under a new version and date.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">Nothing here is advice</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				We write about neurodivergence, cancer, mental health and the environment. None
				of it is medical, psychological, legal or financial advice, and none of it is a
				diagnosis or a treatment plan. It is not a substitute for a professional who
				knows your situation, and it should never be the reason you start, stop or
				change anything about your care.
			</p>
			<p>
				If something here is useful, take it to someone qualified and ask them. If you
				are in immediate danger or crisis, contact your local emergency services rather
				than us &mdash; we are not a crisis service and cannot answer quickly enough to
				be one.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">Registering</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				What happens to the details you give us is set out in{' '}
				<a class="doc__link" href="/privacy">What we hold, and why</a>. These terms add
				three things.
			</p>
			<p>
				Give us details that are true, and that are yours to give. If you are
				registering on someone else&rsquo;s behalf, they should know you are doing it.
			</p>
			<p>
				If you are under eighteen we ask for a parent or guardian, and we write to them
				before we act on the registration. That is not a formality we can waive &mdash;
				the registry itself refuses a registration from a minor that has no guardian on
				it.
			</p>
			<p>
				Registering is not a contract, a membership or a promise of anything from either
				side. It tells us you are interested and how to reach you.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">What you may do, and what you may not</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				Read it, quote it, link to it, print it, and send it to whoever you like. None
				of that needs our permission.
			</p>
			<p>What we ask you not to do:</p>
			<dl class="doc__list">
				<dt>Break it, or try to</dt>
				<dd>
					Probing, overloading, or attempting to reach parts of the system that are not
					offered to you.
				</dd>
				<dt>Register other people without their knowing</dt>
				<dd>
					Or submit details that are false, or that belong to someone who has not asked
					you to.
				</dd>
				<dt>Take it wholesale</dt>
				<dd>
					Automated collection at a scale that costs us to serve, or that copies the
					site rather than reading it.
				</dd>
				<dt>Pass yourself off as us</dt>
				<dd>
					Using our name, our mark or our wording in a way that suggests we said
					something we did not, or that you speak for the Foundation.
				</dd>
			</dl>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">What belongs to whom</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				The site is built from work under several different licences, and they are not
				the same. The full record travels with the code in{' '}
				<code>ATTRIBUTION.md</code>; this is the short version.
			</p>
			<dl class="doc__list">
				<dt>The heron</dt>
				<dd>
					<em>Hummingbird at Arizona-Sonora Desert Museum</em> (2023) by Lorie Shaull, under{
						' '
					}
					<a
						class="doc__link"
						href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"
						rel="noopener">CC BY-SA 4.0</a
					>. We colour-graded and resized it. Because that licence is share-alike, our
					version is offered under the same terms, and anything you make from it has to
					carry the same notice. This binds us as much as it binds you.
				</dd>
				<dt>The Cajal and the Bourgery</dt>
				<dd>
					<em>Purkinje cell of the cerebellum</em> (1899) by Santiago Ram&oacute;n y Cajal,
					and Plate 42 of the <em
						>Trait&eacute; complet de l&rsquo;anatomie de l&rsquo;homme</em
					> (1831&ndash;54), drawn by Nicolas-Henri Jacob for J. M. Bourgery. Both are in
					the public domain. We graded them; the originals belong to everyone.
				</dd>
				<dt>The typefaces</dt>
				<dd>Each under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, and self-hosted.</dd>
				<dt>Everything else</dt>
				<dd>
					Our name, our mark, the project marks, the photography and the words are the
					Foundation&rsquo;s own, and are not licensed for reuse. Ask us if you want to
					use them.
				</dd>
			</dl>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">What we do not promise</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				The site is offered as it is. We do not promise it will always be reachable,
				that every page will be current, or that it will suit any particular purpose of
				yours. We take it down, change it and rewrite it without notice, because it is
				still being built.
			</p>
			<p>
				Where we link to somewhere else, we are pointing rather than vouching. What
				happens on another organisation&rsquo;s site is theirs, including what they do
				with your data.
			</p>
			<p>
				Nothing in these terms limits any liability that the law does not permit us to
				limit &mdash; and nothing in them takes away a right you have under Indian
				consumer or data protection law. Beyond that, we are not liable for loss arising
				from your use of the site.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">Changes, and the law that applies</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				These terms carry a version and a date, at the top of this page. When they
				change materially, both change. We do not quietly edit a live document and leave
				the date alone.
			</p>
			<p>They are governed by the laws of India.</p>
			<p>
				Anything about this page, or the site:{' '}
				<a class="doc__link" href="mailto:hello@itti.org.in">hello@itti.org.in</a>. We
				answer within five working days.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Doc>
